; ted-tabstop-zero-divide (#385): TED accepted the tab size 0 - from
; L:blitzeditor.opts unchecked, from the options requester as typed, and
; a typed value >= 80 became 0 (with a beep) - and every TAB was then a
; divu by 0 (68000 zero divide trap).  blitz2 with a text file "x", tab
; size 0 in the options file; OPTIONS, 100 into the Tab gadget (6) +
; GADGETUP, OK; Tab and "b" typed, SAVE, QUIT (savedefs).  Correct: the
; tab size from the file is clamped to 1, the 100 keeps it, the Tab is
; typed (the text is saved), the saved options have tab size 1; the
; original traps on the Tab (recorded before the fix: TIMEOUT).
; @fixed #385
; @file bo.bas "x\n"
; @source F bo.bas
; @opts tabstop=0
; @expect file bo.bas "b"
; @expect opts blitzeditor.opts tabstop=1
timeout 10
wait req "OKEE DOKEE"
gad 1
wait screen
menu 0 3
wait req "OK" "CANCEL"
str 6 "100"
gad 6
gad 26
wait screen
type "\tb"
menu 0 2
wait freq "Name to save file as"
freq ok
wait screen
menu 0 9
wait exit
